.TH KEPLER'S_HORIZON 1 "2025-12-31" "Version 1.0" "Kepler's Horizon Command Reference"
.SH NAME
kepler \- two-player tactical space combat game command interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kepler
[\fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kepler's Horizon is a two-player tactical game of space combat where players build individualized ships, move them across a hex-based star map, and resolve combat without dice. The objective is to occupy opponent base star hexes and accumulate victory points.

This manual describes all available commands in the Kepler's Horizon command language as defined by the game grammar.

.SH GAME OVERVIEW
.SS Map Components
.TP
.B StarHex
A map hex containing a large or small star (graph node)
.TP
.B BaseStarHex
A map hex containing a large star (6 total: 3 per player)
.TP
.B SpaceHex
A map hex without a star or warpline
.TP
.B WarpLine
Bi-directional edges connecting stars for instantaneous travel

.SS Ship Types
.TP
.B WarpShip (W#)
Ships capable of interstellar travel via warplines
.TP
.B SystemShip (S##)
Ships that cannot travel between stars unless carried by WarpShips

.SH GAME SEQUENCE
Each player-turn consists of the following phases in order:
.PP
.RS
1. Count Victory Points
.br
2. Build Ships (receive BP in Advanced scenario)
.br
3. Movement
.br
4. Resolve Combat
.br
5. SystemShip Pick and Drop
.br
6. End of Turn
.RE

.SH CONCEPTS
.SS Starting a Game
Games are started through the web interface, not via command line:
.PP
.RS
.B 1. Portal
.br
Login or create an account at the web portal.
.PP
.B 2. Lobby
.br
View open rooms or create a new one. Each room can host one game.
.PP
.B 3. Room
.br
Join a room and take a seat (A or B). When both seats are filled, either player can start the game.
.PP
.B 4. Scenario Selection
.br
The room creator selects the scenario:
.RS
.IP \fBlearning\fR
40 BP initial, WarpShips only, 1 base star, first to 1 VP wins
.IP \fBbasic\fR
50 BP initial, WarpShips and SystemShips, 1 base star, first to 2 VP wins
.IP \fBadvanced\fR
20 BP initial + 10 BP/turn, all rules active, 3 base stars, first to 3 VP wins
.RE
.RE

.SH SCENARIOS

.SH COMMANDS

.SS Turn Management Commands
.TP
.B next
Advance the active player to the next phase.
.RS
.PP
\fBSyntax:\fR next
.PP
\fBExample:\fR
.nf
> next
Phase advanced to: Movement
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B done
Complete current player's turn and advance to opponent's first phase.
.RS
.PP
\fBSyntax:\fR done
.PP
\fBExample:\fR
.nf
> done
COMMAND: Your turn has ended. Standing down.
.fi
.RE

.SS Information Commands
.TP
.B status
Show game status and important records (current phase, turn number, BP, VP).
.RS
.PP
\fBSyntax:\fR status
.RE
.TP
.B fleet
Show manifest of your fleet (all ships and their current attributes).
.RS
.PP
\fBSyntax:\fR fleet
.PP
\fBExample:\fR
.nf
> fleet
Your Fleet (Player A):
  W1 The Vanguard  [PD:5 B:3 S:2 T:1 M:6] at SONAL
  W2 The Sentinel  [PD:4 B:2 S:3 T:0 M:0] at UR
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B crt
Display the Combat Results Table
.TP
.B hex \fIlocation\fR
Show location and spatial information about the specified hex
.TP
.B online
Show which players are online and their connection times
.TP
.B stats
Display statistics about the game, your fleet, and opponent
.TP
.B fleet
Show manifest of your fleet (all ships and their current attributes)
.TP
.B system \fIname\fR
Show environmental information about the specified star system
.TP
.B galaxy
Complete overview of all systems and all ships in the game

.SS Turn Management Commands
.TP
.B next
Advance the active player to the next phase
.TP
.B done
Complete current player's turn and advance to opponent's first phase

.SS Build Commands
.TP
.B build
Show current build state (active drafts, available BP)
.TP
.B build new \fIcode\fR \fIname\fR
Create a new ship draft with the specified code (e.g., W1, S01) and name
.TP
.B build drafts
List all pending build drafts
.TP
.B build drafts \fIship_code\fR
Show detailed attributes of a specific draft ship
.TP
.B build set \fIattributes\fR
Set attributes on the current draft ship. Attributes are specified as:
.RS
.TP
.B pd=\fIN\fR or d=\fIN\fR
Power/Drive strength (1 BP per unit, provides movement and combat power)
.TP
.B b=\fIN\fR
Beam weapon strength (1 BP per unit, max power for beam projector)
.TP
.B s=\fIN\fR
Screen strength (1 BP per unit, absorbs hits equal to power + tech level)
.TP
.B t=\fIN\fR
Number of missile tubes (1 BP per tube, requires 1 PD to fire)
.TP
.B m=\fIN\fR
Number of missiles (1 BP per 3 missiles, each does 2 + tech level hits)
.TP
.B sr=\fIN\fR
SystemShip racks (1 BP per rack, WarpShips only, carries 1 SystemShip per rack)
.PP
Example: build set pd=7 b=3 s=2 t=1 m=6
.br
Note: Warp Generator costs 5 BP (automatically added for WarpShips)
.RE
.TP
.B build commit
Commit the current draft, spending BP and adding ship to your fleet
.TP
.B build cancel
Cancel the current draft without spending BP

.SS Deployment Commands
.TP
.B deploy
Show current deployment status for both players
.TP
.B deploy \fIship_code\fR \fIsystem_name\fR
Deploy the specified ship to the specified base star hex (must be your base star)

.SS Movement Commands
.TP
.B move
Show current movement status for all ships
.TP
.B move \fIship_code\fR \fIdestination\fR [\fIwaypoint\fR...]
Move the specified ship to destination, optionally through waypoints. Movement costs:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
1 PD: Move to adjacent hex
.IP \(bu 2
1 PD: Enter warpline at star hex
.IP \(bu 2
1 PD: Travel full warpline to destination star
.IP \(bu 2
1 PD: Pick up one SystemShip
.IP \(bu 2
1 PD: Drop off one SystemShip
.PP
Ships must stop at star hexes occupied by enemy ships.
.br
Ships may freely move through space hexes with enemy ships.
.RE

.SS Combat Commands
.TP
.B combat
Show status of current combat situation
.TP
.B combat order \fIship\fR \fItactic\fR \fItarget\fR \fIallocation\fR
Issue combat orders for a ship. Components:
.RS
.TP
.I ship
Your ship identifier (e.g., W1, S05)
.TP
.I tactic
Combat tactic: \fBattack\fR, \fBdodge\fR, or \fBescape\fR (WarpShips only)
.TP
.I target
Enemy ship identifier to target
.TP
.I allocation
Power allocation from PD to attributes:
.RS
.TP
.B pd=\fIN\fR or d=\fIN\fR
Drive allocation (for maneuver, affects CRT row/column)
.TP
.B b=\fIN\fR
Beam power (cannot exceed built capacity)
.TP
.B s=\fIN\fR
Screen power (cannot exceed built capacity)
.TP
.B t=\fIN\fR
Tubes to power (1 PD per tube)
.TP
.B m=\fIN\fR
Missiles to fire (requires powered tubes)
.PP
Note: Total allocation cannot exceed current PD
.br
Note: Cannot use Beams/Screens and Missiles in same round
.RE
.RE
.TP
.B combat order commit
Commit all combat orders for this round
.TP
.B combat order cancel
Cancel all combat orders and re-issue
.TP
.B combat apply \fIship\fR \fIdamage_allocation\fR
Apply damage hits to ship attributes (defender chooses where hits are taken)
.TP
.B combat apply commit
Commit damage allocation
.TP
.B combat apply cancel
Cancel damage allocation and re-apply

.SS Pick and Drop Commands
.TP
.B pick \fIlocation\fR
Show status of what can be picked up at the specified hex
.TP
.B pick \fIsystemship\fR \fIwarpship\fR
Pick up the specified SystemShip into the specified WarpShip's rack
.TP
.B drop \fIwarpship\fR
List what may be dropped from the specified WarpShip
.TP
.B drop \fIsystemship\fR \fIwarpship\fR
Drop the specified SystemShip from the specified WarpShip at current location

.SS Repair and Resupply Commands
.TP
.B repair
List ships that can be repaired (must be at your base star hex)
.TP
.B repair \fIship_code\fR
Repair the specified ship using BP (1 BP repairs 1 unit of any attribute up to original max)
.TP
.B resupply
Show available BP and resupply capabilities (missiles only)
.TP
.B resupply \fIship_code\fR \fIquantity\fR
Resupply the specified ship with missiles (1 BP per 3 missiles, up to original max)

.SS Help Commands
.TP
.B help
Show help screen and list all help topics
.TP
.B help \fItopic\fR
Show help about a specific topic or command

.SH SHIP ATTRIBUTES
.TP
.B Power/Drive (PD)
Engine strength. Provides movement points and combat power allocation. Cost: 1 BP per unit.
.TP
.B Warp Generator (WG)
Enables interstellar travel and warpline usage. Cost: 5 BP. Required for WarpShips.
.TP
.B Beams (B)
Energy weapon projector. Max strength = BP spent. Cost: 1 BP per unit. Damage = power + tech level.
.TP
.B Screens (S)
Protective energy screen. Absorbs hits = power + tech level. Cost: 1 BP per unit.
.TP
.B Tubes (T)
Missile launchers. Each tube fires 1 missile/round. Requires 1 PD to power. Cost: 1 BP per tube.
.TP
.B Missiles (M)
Projectile weapons. Damage = 2 + tech level. Cost: 1 BP per 3 missiles.
.TP
.B SystemShip Racks (SR)
Carries SystemShips (WarpShips only). 1 SystemShip per rack. Cost: 1 BP per rack.

.SH TECHNOLOGY LEVELS
In Advanced scenario, tech level increases every 4 turns:
.PP
.RS
Turns 1-4: Level 0
.br
Turns 5-8: Level 1
.br
Turns 9-12: Level 2
.br
Turns 13-16: Level 3
.br
(continues +1 per 4 turns)
.RE
.PP
Tech level adds to:
.IP \(bu 2
Beam damage when hitting
.IP \(bu 2
Missile damage when hitting (2 + tech level)
.IP \(bu 2
Screen absorption when powered

.SH COMBAT RESOLUTION
.SS Combat Results Table (CRT)
The CRT determines hit/miss based on:
.IP \(bu 2
Firing ship's tactic (Attack/Dodge/Retreat)
.IP \(bu 2
Target ship's tactic (Attack/Dodge/Retreat)
.IP \(bu 2
Drive difference (Firing Drive - Target Drive)

.SS Combat Tactics
.TP
.B Attack
Aggressive offense. Best hit chance when drive advantage is 0 to +2.
.TP
.B Dodge
Defensive maneuvering. Good hit chance at +1/+2 drive, hard to hit at 0/-1.
.TP
.B Retreat (WarpShips only)
Attempt to escape combat. Must get "Escapes" result against all enemy ships.

.SS Damage Application
.IP 1. 3
Calculate hits from all weapons that hit
.IP 2. 3
Subtract Screen power + tech level (if Screen powered)
.IP 3. 3
Apply remaining "effective hits" to ship attributes (owner chooses where)
.IP 4. 3
Ship destroyed when all attributes except Warp Generator reduced to 0

.SS Special Combat Rules
.IP \(bu 2
Beams and Screens can be used together
.IP \(bu 2
Missiles cannot be used same round as Beams/Screens
.IP \(bu 2
Missiles always use Attack tactic with their own drive setting
.IP \(bu 2
SystemShips cannot Retreat (must be carried by WarpShip)
.IP \(bu 2
Combat ends when: all ships of one side destroyed/retreated, or 3 consecutive rounds with no unabsorbed damage (attacker must withdraw)

.SH MOVEMENT RULES
.IP 1. 3
WarpShips must stop at star hexes occupied by enemy ships
.IP 2. 3
WarpShips may move through space hexes with enemy ships
.IP 3. 3
WarpLines are treated as space hexes for movement
.IP 4. 3
Ships with PD=0 cannot move
.IP 5. 3
PD used for movement is not expended (full PD available for combat)
.IP 6. 3
Cannot move onto enemy base star hex during turn 1

.SH VICTORY CONDITIONS
.TP
.B Dominance Victory
Accumulate required victory points (1/2/3 depending on scenario) by occupying enemy base stars at start of your turn
.TP
.B Elimination Victory
Destroy all enemy ships
.TP
.B Draw
Neither player has effective ships remaining (Learning/Basic scenarios only)

.SH BUILD POINT COSTS
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
